"Yes, and I'll tell you why," he said Monday night. "You don't see it anymore because the runner thinks he has to avoid the catcher. He doesn't. If the guy is in the way you're still able to hit him. We've just retrained the mind so much right there that they look to miss him.
"I much prefer what Riz did there, and what he did was right. Absolutely right.... Nobody could tell me differently. It's a good play.
"The catcher is in the way. You don't try to avoid him in an effort to score and hurt yourself. You hit him, just like Riz did."
