The 14th edition of the Anheuser-Busch Golf Classic at the Kingsmill Golf Club tops the area golf schedule for the 1994 season.
The tournament is set for July 7-10.
''I'm sure we'll have as good a field as we did last year,'' said tournament director Johnnie Bender. ''But we're still stuck with our tournament being held the week before the British Open.''
Jim Gallagher will return to defend his championship. Kingsmill touring pro Curtis Strange and former A-B champ Lanny Wadkins also will be in the field.
Richmond once again will play host to two major tournaments. The Nike Tour returns for the second year for the Nike Dominion Open June 16-19 at the Dominion Club, and the AMF/Signet State Open will be at Willow Oaks Country Club July 14-17.
